# Authoring checklist

Confirm **every** item before opening a change for review. Failure on any item means the
change is not ready.

1. **Design-system primitives** — no ad-hoc `View` + `Text` + `Pressable` compositions in
   product screens; missing primitives were created first.
2. **Token-driven styling** — no new hard-coded hex colors or pixel values.
3. **File structure** — styles in `styled.ts`, pure logic in `*Rules.ts`, component in its
   own folder (no monolith append). See `development/08-file-structure.mdc`.
4. **Layout ownership** — page padding, safe area, and keyboard avoidance are owned by the
   page/modal layout primitive, not re-implemented in the screen.
5. **Typed props** with explicit variant unions; JSDoc on the component, props interface,
   and every hook/callback/effect; anchor comments on non-obvious logic.
6. **Storybook** — stories cover all variants and states (loading, disabled, selected,
   busy, empty, long-content); the story registry is regenerated.
7. **Pure logic extracted** to `*Rules.ts` with colocated tests.
8. **Accessibility** — roles, labels, states, touch targets, focus order
   (`development/05-accessibility.mdc`).
9. **i18n keys** for all user-visible copy, translated in every locale
   (`development/06-internationalization.mdc`).
10. **Security review of the surface** — inputs validated, sensitive data handled per
    `security/02-data-protection.mdc`, deep-link params validated per
    `security/05-navigation-deeplinks.mdc`.
11. **Cross-platform** verified on iOS, Android, Web, and Storybook
    (`development/02-cross-platform.mdc`).
12. **Complexity analysis** for hot paths, lists, animations, and new dependencies
    (`development/07-performance.mdc`).
13. **Documentation** created or updated under the correct `docs/` category and linked from
    its index (`workflow/03-documentation.mdc`).
14. **Quality gates green** — lint, typecheck, and the full Jest suite
    (`workflow/01-quality-gates.mdc`).
